course: dictionary
lesson: 9353
title: Splice: joining things together
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: To splice means to join two things firmly so they become one piece. You can splice two ropes by weaving their ends together, or splice two film clips so they play one after the other. A splice is the place where the two things meet.
explain: The word also turns up in grammar. «It was raining, we went inside.» This is a comma splice: two complete sentences are stuck together with only a comma. The clue is that both sides could stand alone as sentences.
explain: Look at the words around splice to find its meaning. «Scientists splice genes» means they cut and join pieces of DNA. «Get spliced» is an old, informal British phrase, so the context tells you it has nothing to do with ropes.
fact: To splice means to join two things together firmly.
fact: A splice is the place where two things have been joined.
fact: Splicing rope means weaving the strands at its ends into each other.
fact: «Splice together» means joining two pieces so they play one after the other, as in film.
fact: «Get spliced» is informal British slang meaning to get married.
exercise: In «To splice two ropes, weave their ends together», what does splice mean? | *To join two things firmly | To cut something into tiny pieces | To paint a wall | To break a rope in half
exercise: «It was raining, we went inside.» What is wrong with this sentence? | It has no comma | It is too short | It uses the word raining | *Two complete sentences are joined only by a comma
exercise: «Get spliced» is an old British phrase. What does it mean? | *To get married | To make a film | To go sailing | To tie a rope
test: Scientists use gene ___ to change living things. What word fits the gap? | *Splicing | Splashing | Spelling | Sailing
test: Which is a correct way to fix «It was raining, we went inside.»? | *It was raining, so we went inside. | It was raining, we went inside, we got wet. | It was, raining, we went inside. | It was raining we went inside.
exam: Which sentence uses splice to mean join two film clips? | Ali splices the bread into thin slices. | Ali splices the wet paint off the fence. | Ali splices a cup of tea for his nan. | *Ali splices the two film clips so they play in order.
